WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:08.670
Hi, I'm Brunchandama. I'm a lead design engineer walking on Millicoat. So what is Millicoat?

2
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:18.270
It basically is a form of microarchitecture that runs on IBMC. And by microarchitecture, I mean, there's a

3
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:20.990
layer

4
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:26.190
invisible layer between what we publish in the principles of operations and

5
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.670
another layer which is a microarchitecture. And

6
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:36.550
And the reason why we have that is because every generation of z, the microarchitecture changes.

7
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:42.070
However, what we publish in the principles of operation, that does not change. We add stuff,

8
00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:47.190
we don't remove stuff. We add new instructions, we don't remove instructions. So an instruction

9
00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:53.590
that we introduced 10 years ago, functionally it does the same thing, but microarchitecture,

10
00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:59.110
really how we get to that answer is very different. And in Millicoat, we make those changes so

11
00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:03.110
that the operating system or the user of the program doesn't have to make those changes.

12
00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:10.310
In addition to the instruction set, the implemented instruction set on the principle of operations,

13
00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:17.430
Millicoat is also involved in a few other key aspects of IBMC. We do system initialization,

14
00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:22.710
which basically means you pull an on the system, going to the IML steps, initial machine load,

15
00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:29.190
that's IML. Millicoat is involved with virtualization. So you have a single resource, a system,

16
00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:33.270
and you're going to divide it up into logical partitions and run different operating systems

17
00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.590
in each partition. For that, to be possible, you need an instruction that's called

18
00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:43.270
psi or start interpretive execution, and that instruction is implemented in Millicoat.

19
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:48.150
So that's Millicoat in a nutshell. As you can see, the things that we do on the system is

20
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:55.190
important, especially for recovery, for availability, and for serviceability. I've been enjoying

21
00:01:55.190 --> 00:02:06.790
my work in Millicoat, and it's been fun joining so far. Thank you.
